      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "With a single parenteral introduction of thyrocalcitonin (TCT) the algesthesia of soft tissues (tall skin, paw) is moderately increasing, while the algesic action of morphine and promedol against the background of TCT-gets weaker. And contrarywise algesthesia of hard tissues of the tooth becomes significantly lower under the effect of TCT and this continues for a long time."},
